.TH SIGSUSPEND 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sigsuspend \- temporarily replaces the signal mask with the eight-byte linux kernel signal set and waits for a signal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <signal.h>
.B int sigsuspend(const sigset_t* mask);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Temporarily replaces the signal mask with the eight-byte Linux kernel signal set and waits for a signal.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sigsuspend (2)
